From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:32:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: count depth and stencil samples once in GMEM

A resource's layout.cpp already includes its sample count. Multiplying it
by the framebuffer sample count again overestimates depth/stencil storage
for MSAA. Recover the per-sample size before accounting for the framebuffer
samples, including multisampled render-to-texture and separate stencil.

Split from Jetha Chan's Mesa 26.2.6 port of the MIT-licensed
justhalfbit/thinksmart-ubuntu-image GMEM fix. Keep the Lineage-selected
Mesa version and apply this independently of experimental FP16 changes.

Origin: Jetha Chan's ThinkSmart View port, adapted to Lineage Mesa 26.2.3
Source: https://github.com/jethac/lenovo-thinksmart-view/blob/1f99f7f09c26074d53064d7bb1fada262cbef10a/streams/audio-dsp/patches/0001-freedreno-gmem-no-fit-sysmem.patch
Original-commit: 712ef9414fa111d1a7fd2a1134b217b32de09f46
Base-commit: 400e673cf8ba515d3aace56ed3acc3bb300869a5
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -462,9 +462,16 @@ gmem_key_init(struct fd_batch *batch, bool assume_zs, bool no_scis_opt)
 
    if (has_zs || assume_zs) {
       struct fd_resource *rsc = fd_resource(pfb->zsbuf.texture);
-      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+      /* layout.cpp already includes the resource's sample count.  What
+       * takes space in GMEM is the framebuffer's sample count (they differ
+       * for multisampled-render-to-texture), so scale the per-sample size.
+       */
+      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp / fd_resource_nr_samples(&rsc->b.b) *
+                          pfb->samples;
       if (rsc->stencil)
-         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp /
+                             fd_resource_nr_samples(&rsc->stencil->b.b) *
+                             pfb->samples;
 
       /* If we clear z or s but not both, and we are using z24s8 (ie.
        * !separate_stencil) then we need to restore the other, even if
